# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal data — NEVER commit.
#
# Note the `private/*` + negation form. `private/` alone would exclude the
# DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory —
# `!private/.gitkeep` would silently do nothing. Same reason for matches/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
private/*
!private/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output and run state. Regenerated by every scan; per-operator, not project data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
matches/*
!matches/.gitkeep
resources/scan-history.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups. Version control replaced the project-FILE .bak-{date} convention, which
# was retired on 2026-09-04 — a tracked file's history is its backup.
#
# It does NOT replace the tracker backup jobscan_tracker.save() writes inside private/:
# that directory is gitignored, so the trackers are in no repo either way. That copy is
# the pre-write state, and it is what you restore from when a post-write assertion fires
# on a file os.replace has already swapped in. save() keeps the newest few and prunes
# the rest, so they no longer pile up.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
#
# .venv/ is per-machine: every clone builds its own from requirements.txt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
